    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n177" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄβρομος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span> collect.) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>joining in a shout,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.41
			</span></i>; taken by <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> to mean <i>noisy</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>
			intens.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span> priv.) <i>noiseless,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.153
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄβρωμος.</span>
			
		</div>
